WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.170
Yoyoyo. Yoyoyo.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.600
What separates great AI videos from
mediocre ones?

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.840
The simple answer is great image
references.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.120
The difference between a good generation
and a bad one starts before you

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.780
write the video prompt. It starts with
creating your assets.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:33.290
Welcome back. Today, we're going deeper
into a professional AI

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:37.580
workflow, creating the characters and
locations for your video.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:42.500
First, I want to show you four videos
created from images generated with

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:47.560
different models. Look closely and you'll
notice a significant difference.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:52.220
All of the videos were generated in
Seedance 2.5 using the same two prompts.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:56.330
This video model smooths out even the most
obvious AI slop, but it doesn't

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.900
eliminate it completely, so the quality of
your assets still plays a crucial

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:04.000
role. For these videos, I created the
assets with four models.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.560
Soul 2.0, Soul Cinema, GPT Image 2.5,

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:11.860
Sunburst, and Nano Banana Pro.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.820
The image quality speaks for itself.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.340
You can see the difference in the finished
videos.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:21.620
To understand where it comes from, let's
go back to the original images.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:25.560
We'll compare the lighting, the textures,
and the sense of depth.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:29.580
Images from the Soul models truly seem to
have more Soul and a more cinematic

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:34.600
feel, while Nano Banana and GPT look more
like standard AI-generated images.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:38.670
You can spot repeating patterns in the
grass, distracting reflections on the

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:43.730
tiles, excessive image sharpness, lack of
depth, and the color which will

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.380
completely shape the look of your final
video.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:51.590
Most importantly, generating the images
with the Soul models costs 24 times

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:55.480
less. Once you learn to see these
differences, you'll be a step ahead of the

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:59.720
average AI creator, and your generations
will reach a whole new level.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:03.750
The goal of this lesson is to teach you
how to recognize these differences

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:08.330
and show you the tools you can use to
achieve this level of

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:10.070
quality.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:17.290
So where do we start? First, we'll cast
our characters, create the

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:19.640
locations, and then refine both.

