00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:38.900
Let's start with Soul Cinema, our own
model.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:44.000
It's especially good at giving locations a
cinematic feel, convincing light,

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:47.740
natural textures, and the sense that
you're looking at a frame from a real

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:50.810
film. When you're creating images that
will later be used for video

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:56.100
generation, you want smooth, high-quality
textures, a wide tonal range, and

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.980
preserved detail in both highlights and
shadows.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:03.690
The color of the image is just as
important because it will directly shape

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.460
the color palette of your final video.

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:10.710
Lighting matters too. The light sources
and direction provide important

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.620
context for the video model.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:15.640
If the shadows in your image suggest that
the light is coming from above,

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:19.310
even when no light source is visible in
the frame, the generated video will

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:21.660
preserve that same overhead lighting
direction.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:25.100
With Soul Cinema, you'll never doubt that
a landscape or location could

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:29.130
exist in real life. Like any other model,
Soul Cinema has its own

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:31.800
limitations and weaknesses.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:36.160
First, it supports only two modes,
generating from a text prompt, text to

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.660
image, or generating from a single image
with no option to add a prompt and

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:44.060
guide the result. This second method is
called image to image.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:47.780
I'll explain its superpower in the PDF
attached to this lesson.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:52.420
Second, generations can contain broken
objects or illogical details that

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:55.980
feel unnatural in the frame or are simply
visual clutter.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:59.780
If you look closely at evening or
nighttime scenes, you'll notice the

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:03.420
shadows can get so dark that you lose all
the detail.

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:06.340
And generating a video won't bring that
detail back.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.480
Those areas will stay solid black.

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:12.540
Soul Cinema also isn't as strong at prompt
following as the other models in

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:17.540
this lesson. Prompt following simply means
how precisely a model follows

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:22.440
your instructions. For example, imagine
asking for a sofa in the center of

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:26.160
the room and a window on the right.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:31.000
GPT image will follow that composition in
almost every generation.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.690
Soul Cinema, by contrast, tends to add its
own creativity and

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:37.220
interpretation, slightly changing your
brief.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:40.840
Despite these limitations, Soul Cinema
remains the most realistic and

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:44.940
lifelike model available. Learn to work
around its weaknesses and it can

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.080
deliver the highest quality images.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.200
It's also extremely affordable.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:54.540
Generating one image costs just 0.125
credits, so you can create

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.740
8 images for a single credit.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:06:00.250
All the prompts used for these generations
will be included in the lesson

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:04.130
PDF. You'll also find a large language
model skill file in the lesson

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:08.400
materials. You can upload it to your chat
or app or use it directly in

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:13.010
supercomputer. This skill will help you
achieve top tier results with almost

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.120
any generative image model.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:18.580
What if we need a fantasy or sci-fi world?

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:23.800
For those larger, more complex
environments, we often turn to Seedream
5.0

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.160
Pro. Look at these examples.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:29.820
There's a whole city built inside a huge
cylindrical structure and a

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:32.780
landscape with giant eyes emerging beneath
